"""Keep human-facing pitch, script and Q&A quantities tied to measured artifacts."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def load(p):return json.loads((ROOT/p).read_text())
b=load('results.json');c=load('reports/v3_c_results.json');bound=load('reports/wrong_clear_bounds.json')['seeds']['v3_c'];live=load('reports/live_smoke.json');bench=load('reports/benchmark_current_reader.json')
percent=lambda v:f'{v*100:.2f}%'
problem=(ROOT/'README.md').read_text().split('\n> ',1)[1].split('\n',1)[0]
qa=[
('How is this different from invoice matching?','It reconciles declarations with material/power proxies, movement, supplier returns and bank flows. There is no benchmark against commercial fraud systems and no claim that the approach is unprecedented.'),
('Is this a machine-learning fraud classifier?','No. Six deterministic SQL checks form four source families. SQL flags a month when at least two families fire. An optional LLM can explain evidence only; displayed notes use the deterministic fallback.'),
('What are the primary and confirmation results?',f"V3-B monthly recall {percent(b['factory_month']['recall'])}, FPR {percent(b['factory_month']['fpr'])}, precision {percent(b['factory_month']['precision'])}. V3-C monthly recall {percent(c['factory_month']['recall'])}, FPR {percent(c['factory_month']['fpr'])}, precision {percent(c['factory_month']['precision'])}. All are synthetic and have factory-cluster intervals in the artifacts."),
('Why trust synthetic results?','They allow recovery of known planted scenarios to be measured. Held-out seeds share the same generator; intervals do not cover generator bias or real-taxpayer error. They do not establish operational accuracy.'),
('How was calibration done?',f"V3-A alone selected threshold {b['protocol']['threshold']} and K={b['factory_queue']['k']}. B and C use frozen choices. No new threshold was tuned in the judge audit; a stale live setting was repaired to the already-published value."),
('What did the audit discover in Live mode?','The schema default had been 0.10 while offline evaluation used 0.05. A user-approved settings-only repair restored 0.05. Every live monthly signal count and flag now matches saved V3-C, and API health rejects mismatched live decisions.'),
('What does the factory queue mean?',f"A factory enters after at least K={c['factory_queue']['k']} prioritised months. V3-C queue size {c['factory_queue']['queue_size']}; recall {percent(c['factory']['recall'])}, FPR {percent(c['factory']['fpr'])}, precision {percent(c['factory']['precision'])}. This differs from monthly classification."),
('What is the top-50 precision?',f"Monthly macro precision is {percent(c['precision_at_k']['50']['macro_precision'])}. The generator has no active cheats in Jan–Mar, whose small returned queues are false alarms; Apr–Dec each reach 100% in the top 50. This is a synthetic monthly snapshot statistic, not measured weekly effectiveness."),
('Why is zero wrong-clears not proof of safety?',f"Zero events span {bound['active_cheat_factories']} active-cheat factories and {bound['active_cheat_months']} active cheat months in C. Approximate factory-level rule-of-three upper bound is {percent(bound['approximate_upper_95'])}, assuming independent factories. Verification labels come from the generator; sophisticated forgers and cluster-bootstrap wrong-clear intervals remain untested."),
('What does Exasol actually do?','Exasol Personal is the primary database for joins, aggregates, stock/baseline windows, reconciliation views, source-family prioritisation and guarded follow-up SELECTs. Loop links are evidence context; loop-only/ring detection is not implemented. UDF and MCP execution are not demonstrated.'),
('Was Exasol faster than DuckDB?',f"No in the current recorded comparison: stock medians Exasol {bench['checks']['stock_rollforward']['exasol_median_seconds']:.3f}s, DuckDB {bench['checks']['stock_rollforward']['duckdb_median_seconds']:.3f}s. Counts and gap sums match. Current dataset: {bench['current_factories']:,} factories, {bench['current_feature_rows']:,} feature rows. Physical plans and load coverage differ. The 20.98M-row run is historical."),
('What are the current Live and security results?',f"The current guarded API smoke passed all three intents, notes, activity, injection/unknown-intent rejection and {live['parallel_ask']['queries']} parallel questions. Measured p95 {live['parallel_ask']['p95_seconds']:.3f}s includes the new protocol validation. The reader cannot read database truth. Public Pages always uses recorded snapshots; real power/bank access would require lawful privacy controls.")]
(ROOT/'docs/judge_qa.md').write_text('# Judge Q&A — current V3 evidence\n\nGenerated by scripts/build_submission_text.py from results.json and the named reports. All data is synthetic.\n\n'+'\n\n'.join(f'{i}. **{q}** {a}' for i,(q,a) in enumerate(qa,1))+'\n')
script=f'''# Demo recording script — owner: Kushagra Gupta

**Status: video not recorded by this assistant; user will create it. Required maximum: three minutes.** This script targets 2:45. All quantities below come from the current artifact files. Public Pages uses recorded examples; a local API can execute the guarded follow-ups live. Always state which mode is shown.

## 0:00–0:20 — Problem

Display the exact statement; do not try to read every word at speed:

> {problem}

Say: “GST Evidence gives an officer a review list when declarations contradict evidence from other sources.”

## 0:20–1:00 — Caught cheat

Open Cases, choose Caught cheat: F000902, 2026-05. Show the source families, expected/observed/gap rows and validated deterministic note. Explain that SQL determines priority and the note explains evidence. Every record is synthetic.

## 1:00–1:25 — Honest exception and a miss

Choose Honest exception: F000016, 2026-04. Show the generated verification record supporting its machinery change. Choose Miss: F000025, 2026-08; only movement fires, so the planted cheat is review-only. Verification itself is simulated.

## 1:25–1:50 — Ask and inspect SQL

Choose “Dispatch gap by month”. Show the fixed SELECT and returned evidence. Public site: say “recorded response”. Local verified API: say “executed now through the restricted reader”. Do not claim an MCP or LLM live demo.

## 1:50–2:20 — Results and actual performance

Choose V3-C. Monthly recall {percent(c['factory_month']['recall'])}; false-positive rate {percent(c['factory_month']['fpr'])}. V3-A froze threshold {c['protocol']['threshold']} and K={c['factory_queue']['k']}. C missed {c['factory_month']['fn']} active cheat months. Wrong-clears are zero of {bound['active_cheat_factories']} active-cheat factories, with approximate upper bound {percent(bound['approximate_upper_95'])} under an independence assumption, using generated verification labels. System shows {bench['current_feature_rows']:,} current feature rows and an honest DuckDB comparison; the large historical workload is not a fresh run.

## 2:20–2:45 — Limits and close

Synthetic only. Human review, not an enforcement decision. Forger testing, ablation/wrong-clear intervals, second-machine reproduction and a fresh full-scale load remain open. Lawful access to tax, power and bank data is future work. Germany is only an unvalidated possible adaptation, with no figures or deployment claimed.

## Before uploading

Use a screen recording of the actual public or local site; keep the mode label visible. Check duration, sound and source figures. Do not use a stale MP4 or simulate a query. Put the final user-recorded video URL in SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md and confirm its access permissions. The assistant has not submitted the portal form.
'''
(ROOT/'docs/demo_script.md').write_text(script)
(ROOT/'docs/PITCH_CONTENT.md').write_text('# Current deck content and sources\n\nThe editable PPTX and PDF in deliverables/ use V3-B/V3-C, threshold 0.05 and K=3. The source deck under legacy/submission/ is obsolete and must not be submitted.\n\n'+ '\n\n'.join(f'**{q}**\n\n{a}' for q,a in qa)+'\n')
print('Updated recording script, judge Q&A and pitch source notes.')
